WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.559
Leases. Loans. Job offers.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.996
Pages of fine print, and one signature.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.096
This is Brief: every clause, explained.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.037
The terms that cost you money are buried in dense text.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.870
A chatbot might guess, and a guess in a contract is dangerous.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.599
Brief shows the exact words behind every answer.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.107
Sign in with Google, and your dashboard shows every document, and what needs attention.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.808
Add a PDF, a scan, or up to five phone photos, and Brief reads it into numbered clauses.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.536
Open a document, and the key terms appear, each with its quote.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.601
Click one, and the exact words light up in the clause.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.512
Before you sign lists the questions people forget to ask, and flags what the document leaves out.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.918
Copy the summary, download a PDF, or add the dates to your calendar.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.713
Now ask a question in plain words.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.314
Brief finds the right clauses by meaning and by keywords, then Gemini writes the answer.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.418
Code checks every quote against the clause, and shows only what it can prove.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.717
If the document does not say, Brief says so.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.388
Under the hood, a Next.js website talks to a FastAPI service.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.259
Postgres with pgvector stores the clauses, and Gemini does the language work.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.916
It runs on Vercel and Render, and GitHub Actions tests every change.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.919
Brief explains what a document says. It is not legal advice.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.662
Brief. Every clause, explained, at briefcontracts.com.
